# alias: OptimisticMinimum
# button-text: Optimistic Minimum
# gib-works: true
# bba-works: true
# scenario-title: --- Optimistic Minimum
# auction-filter: Auction.....\n(1H +Pass +2N.* Pass\n4H|1S +Pass +2N.* Pass\n4S|1N +Pass +2C.* Pass\n2[HS]|1N +Pass +2[DH].* Pass\n[23][HS]|1N +Pass +4[DH].* Pass\n4[HS]|1[CD] +Pass +1H +Pass\n2H|1[CD] +Pass +1S +Pass\n2S)
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-DEFAULT
# convention-card-ew: 21GF-GIB

/*@chat
--- Optimistic Minimum
Partner's bidding has limited their hand. You must decide: stop in game, or bid on toward slam?
  1M - 2N (Jacoby) - 4M -- opener is minimum (12-14), no shortness. You have 15-18.
  1N - 2C - 2M -- a 4-4 fit opposite 15-17. You have 13-16 with shortness.
  1N - transfer (or Texas) - M -- opposite 15-17. You have a 6-card major, 12-15, with shortness.
  1m - 1M - 2M -- opener is minimum (12-14) with 4-card support. You have 15-18.
Picture partner's "Optimistic Minimum":
  1. Visualize partner's shape.
  2. Give partner only the HCP their bidding promised.
  3. Put those HCP where they help you most (aces, trump honors, kings in your long suits, nothing opposite your shortness).
  4. If slam is good opposite that hand, and still reasonable opposite a less-perfect one, bid on.
4NT is Roman Keycard Blackwood (1430).
Based on Robert Todd, Advinbridge "This Week in Bridge" #652.
@chat*/

dealer north

#include "script/Predict-Opening-1-Bid-North"
#include "script/Calm-Opponents"
#include "script/TP"

##### Type 1: 1M - 2N (Jacoby) - 4M #####
# North opens 1M with a minimum, semi-balanced hand -> 4M over Jacoby 2N
# Good second suits -- 5+ cards with 2 of the top 3 (these would bid 4x over 2N)
gS = spades(north)>4   and top3(north,spades)>1
gH = hearts(north)>4   and top3(north,hearts)>1
gD = diamonds(north)>4 and top3(north,diamonds)>1
gC = clubs(north)>4    and top3(north,clubs)>1

fitSpades = oneSpade and spades(south)>3
fitHearts = oneHeart and hearts(south)>3
fit = fitSpades or fitHearts

secondSuit = (fitSpades and (gH or gD or gC)) or (fitHearts and (gS or gD or gC))
nShort     = shape(north, any 0xxx + any 1xxx)
minimumOpener = fit and suitPoints>11 and suitPoints<15 and not (secondSuit or nShort)

# South bids Jacoby 2N with slam interest; no long side suit to show first
lenSouth = fitSpades ? spades(south) : hearts(south)
strSouth = tpSouth + lenSouth - 4
j2nSouth = hcp(south)>14 and hcp(south)<19 and strSouth<23 and (hcp(north)+hcp(south))>26
noSideSuit = not shape(south, any 6xxx + any 7xxx)

typeJ2N = minimumOpener and j2nSouth and noSideSuit

##### Shared by the 1NT types #####
sShort = shape(south, any 0xxx + any 1xxx)

##### Type 2: 1N - 2C - 2M (4-4 fit) #####
# South has exactly one 4-card major and shortness; North shows that major
stayH = hearts(south)==4 and spades(south)<4 and hearts(north)>3
stayS = spades(south)==4 and hearts(south)<4 and spades(north)>3 and hearts(north)<4
typeStayman = oneNT and (stayH or stayS) and sShort and hcp(south)>12 and hcp(south)<17

##### Type 3: 1N - transfer (2D/2H or Texas 4D/4H) - M #####
# South has a 6-card major, shortness, and slam interest opposite 15-17
xferH = hearts(south)==6 and spades(south)<4
xferS = spades(south)==6 and hearts(south)<4
typeTransfer = oneNT and (xferH or xferS) and sShort and hcp(south)>11 and hcp(south)<16

##### Type 4: 1m - 1M - 2M (opener's minimum raise) #####
# South responds in the longer major (hearts with 4-4); North raises with 4-card support
# A strong 5-card major would jump shift, and a longer minor would be bid first
respH = hearts(south)>3 and hearts(south)>=spades(south) and not shape(south, 55xx)
respS = spades(south)>3 and not respH
lenM  = respH ? hearts(south) : spades(south)
topM  = respH ? top3(south,hearts) : top3(south,spades)
quietMajor = (lenM==4 or (lenM==5 and topM<2)) and diamonds(south)<lenM and clubs(south)<lenM
raiseH = respH and hearts(north)==4
raiseS = respS and spades(north)==4
typeRaise = (oD or oC) and (raiseH or raiseS) and quietMajor and hcp(north)>11 and hcp(north)<15 and hcp(south)>14 and hcp(south)<19

##### Hand types #####
HandType_J2N      = typeJ2N
HandType_Stayman  = typeStayman
HandType_Transfer = typeTransfer
HandType_Raise    = typeRaise

### BEGIN GENERATED LEVELING ###
noLeveling = 1
levelTheDeal = noLeveling
### END GENERATED LEVELING ###

##### Now do it #####
(HandType_J2N or HandType_Stayman or HandType_Transfer or HandType_Raise) and levelTheDeal and calmOpps

produce 30
action
average "1. J2N      " 100 * typeJ2N,
average "2. Stayman  " 100 * typeStayman,
average "3. Transfer " 100 * typeTransfer,
average "4. Raise    " 100 * typeRaise,
